# W0-T23. Three files here are *generated* — each is a pure function of inputs that cannot
# themselves conflict. A line merge on any of them is meaningless at best and wrong at worst, so
# git is told not to attempt one, and the resolution is to recompute the file.
#
# This is narrower than "these files are append-only". A keep-both merge driver on an append-shaped
# file is the trap this task exists to avoid: run on README.md during the #150/#151/#152 session it
# was right on five hunks and wrong on two, because the Layout table looks append-shaped and is
# actually a modification. Recomputing discards both sides, so that failure cannot occur here.
#
# The drivers are registered per clone by `scripts/setup-git.sh`. A clone that has not run it
# conflicts the ordinary way and the fix is to run the render command by hand — it fails toward a
# conflict, never toward a silent bad merge. CI never depends on the drivers; the drift tests are
# what make a stale generated file fail.

memory/LONG_TERM.md merge=regen-memory
pnpm-lock.yaml       merge=relock -diff linguist-generated
